  "review_checks": [
    "Each tap chooses a face from its world-space ray and fetches a clamped texel on that face. Six-layer validation bounds the whole cube group.",
    "The fetched texel-center ray determines the conversion from stored view-axis depth to radial blocker distance. The receiver is intersected with its geometric plane on the same ray.",
    "Reverse-Z receiver bias is converted to a positive radial distance offset before comparisons. PCF performs at most nine texture reads and PCSS at most fifty.",
    "The sign-based orthonormal basis keeps the denominator magnitude at least one. The previous near-negative-Z loss of precision is covered by the production-include test.",
    "LightingPS computes screen derivatives of reconstructed position before its background branch. Its finite normalized geometric normal is passed to local sampling.",
    "The independent boundary sweep covers every face, 256 and 2048 resolution, reverse depths zero/one/interior, zero and large finite radii, PCF/PCSS, zero and axis normals, invalid radii and incomplete cube groups."
  ],
  "resolved_during_review": [
    {
      "issue": "Near-negative-Z division by one plus Z amplified the tangent basis and sampling kernel.",
      "before": "The same private production-include test failed its bounded pixel-span assertion.",
      "after": "The sign-based basis passes the private regression and the production test covers both poles."
    }
  ],
